  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "$-54\\text{ mod }7=${{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The residue of $-54$ modulo $7$ is the integer $0\\le r<7$ such that\n\n$$\n-54≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $-54$ as an integer multiple of $7,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $-54≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ because\n\n$$\n-54=(-8)\\cdot 7+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-54$ modulo $7$ is $2.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the addition property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-54 & ≡-54+0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡-54+8\\cdot 7 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡-54+56 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡2 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-54$ modulo $7$ is $2.$",
